#NEXUS

[ paulina-carabajal2019a_fig6: Theropod braincase tree, read by eye. Averostra is a three-way node (Sinosaurus, Ceratosauria, Tetanurae). NEOTHEROPODA, AVEROSTRA, CERATOSAURIA and TETANURAE label nodes and are kept; SAUROPODOMORPHA and COELUROSAURIA sit on the terminal branches of Plateosaurus and Alioramus and are not encoded. The braincase images are not tips. 12 tips, 1 polytomies (3 children); 4 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 8 case (census 2, seed 20261251). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=12;
    TAXLABELS
        Plateosaurus
        Megapnosaurus
        Zupaysaurus
        Sinosaurus
        Ceratosaurus
        Majungasaurus
        Sinraptor
        Allosaurus
        Acrocanthosaurus
        Carcharodontosaurus
        Giganotosaurus
        Alioramus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE paulina-carabajal2019a_fig6 = [&R] (Plateosaurus,(Megapnosaurus,(Zupaysaurus,(Sinosaurus,(Ceratosaurus,Majungasaurus)Ceratosauria,((Sinraptor,(Allosaurus,(Acrocanthosaurus,(Carcharodontosaurus,Giganotosaurus)))),Alioramus)Tetanurae)Averostra))Neotheropoda);
END;
